1
00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:02,860
She felt his warm breath..."

2
00:00:02,862 --> 00:00:04,492
(Leonard:)You will not believe
what Stephen Hawking just said.

3
00:00:04,497 --> 00:00:06,327
PENNY: Get out!
BERNADETTE:
Not now!

4
00:00:17,977 --> 00:00:20,947
(Amelia:)Is the water warm enough?

5
00:00:20,947 --> 00:00:24,717
(Cooper:)Given the fact that you took
the time to build a wood fire,

6
00:00:24,717 --> 00:00:27,147
(Cooper:)draw the water from
the well and heat it,

7
00:00:27,153 --> 00:00:28,883
(Cooper:)it would be rude
to complain.

8
00:00:31,057 --> 00:00:34,527
(Cooper:)But since you asked,
it's a little nippy.

9
00:00:34,527 --> 00:00:36,627
(Amelia:)I can fix that.

10
00:00:41,734 --> 00:00:46,174
(Amelia:)I couldn't help but notice
your unusual undergarments.

11
00:00:46,172 --> 00:00:48,372
(Cooper:)They're not undergarments.

12
00:00:48,374 --> 00:00:50,204
(Cooper:)They're Underoos.

13
00:00:52,378 --> 00:00:54,208
(Cooper:)Where I come from,
they're known as

14
00:00:54,214 --> 00:00:56,784
"underwear that's fun to wear."

15
00:00:57,984 --> 00:01:01,554
(Amelia:)And what's the significance
of the spider?

16
00:01:01,554 --> 00:01:04,154
(Cooper:)Oh, that represents
Spider-Man.

17
00:01:04,157 --> 00:01:07,227
(Cooper:)He does whatever
a spider can.

18
00:01:08,895 --> 00:01:12,565
(Amelia:)There's a lot of rhyming
in the future, isn't there?

19
00:01:12,565 --> 00:01:14,065
LEONARD:
You're right.

20
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:16,567
(Leonard(in bed):)This is even weirder
than I thought.

21
00:01:16,569 --> 00:01:18,699
(Penny:)You want me to
stop reading?

22
00:01:18,705 --> 00:01:20,075
(Leonard:)Are you kidding?
No, no.

23
00:01:21,441 --> 00:01:24,641
"As he stood for
Amelia to dry him..."

24
00:01:29,549 --> 00:01:31,779
(Amelia:)So, tell me, Cooper...

25
00:01:31,784 --> 00:01:36,754
(Amelia:)are the ways of physical love
different in the future?

26
00:01:36,756 --> 00:01:39,826
(Leonard:)Yeah, okay, I'm good.

